note Outline to Symbol. One level of nesting into modules, namespaces, classes, interfaces and impls (kinds 2, 3, 5, 11 and 19), like the tree-sitter resolver. Servers start a symbol at its doc comment or attributes and tree-sitter at the declaration, so the symbol starts on the line of its name (the selection range) and both backends agree on the start that anchors are relative to; a range ending at column 0 stops on the line before. It also records where each name sits, so the call-hierarchy request can point at it.

