note The walk and the cache check. A cache hit keeps the cached file and fills in its text; a miss is parsed with tree-sitter. A file whose language has a server and whose symbols did not come from one is marked pending, and so is a cached server answer that points at lines in a file that changed. Files are sorted by path, linked once, and the cache is saved when anything was parsed or a cached file is gone. Returns the index with each file's modification stamp, which the GUI's watcher compares against the disk.

